/-! # Invertible modules on arbitrary opens of affine space

Source: Stacks Project, Divisors, Tag 0BDA, `lemma-open-subscheme-UFD`, final sentence
(blueprint: lem-sfb-affine-space-open-invertible-trivial).
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules

/-- Every invertible module on any open subscheme of affine space over a field is
isomorphic to its structure sheaf. The open may be empty or nonaffine, the dimension
may be zero, and the field need not be algebraically closed.

Source: Stacks Project, Divisors, Tag 0BDA, `lemma-open-subscheme-UFD`, final sentence
(blueprint: lem-sfb-affine-space-open-invertible-trivial).

Proof:
1. Put A = F[t₁, ..., tₙ] and X = Spec A. Every ideal of F is zero or generated by 1,
so F is Noetherian (`def-weil-pbc-noetherian-ring`). The identity finite-type
presentation and `lem-weil-pbc-finite-type-algebra-noetherian` make A Noetherian.
The single affine cover X makes X locally Noetherian (`pqf-def-locnoeth`). The ring
A is a UFD by `lem-sfb-polynomial-field-ufd`.
2. By clause (c) of `lem-weil-pbc-affine-open-stalk-localization`, the stalk of X at
x is A localized at the corresponding prime. It is a UFD by
`lem-sfb-ufd-prime-localizations`. This holds in particular at every point outside V.
3. Apply `lem-sfb-invertible-extension-factorial-complement` to extend L to an
invertible module L' on X, with an isomorphism a : L'|_V ≅ L. Its hypotheses are
steps 1 and 2; no density, affineness, or nonemptiness of V is required.
4. By `lem-sfb-affine-space-invertible-trivial`, choose b : L' ≅ O_X. Restriction
preserves the identities and compositions expressing that b and its inverse are
inverse. Since O_X|_V = O_V by `def-weil-open-immersion`, compose a⁻¹ with b|_V
to get L ≅ O_V. The same argument includes the empty open and n = 0. -/
theorem nonempty_iso_unit_of_open_mvPolynomial_field (F : Type u) [Field F] (n : ℕ)
    (V : (Spec (CommRingCat.of (MvPolynomial (Fin n) F))).Opens)
    (L : V.toScheme.Modules) [L.IsInvertible] :
    Nonempty (L ≅ Scheme.Modules.unit V.toScheme) := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules
